.TH ACPI 8
.SH NAME
acpi \- Advanced Configuration and Power Interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I (in plan9.ini)
.B *acpi=
.PP
.B aux/acpi
[
.B -H
]
[
.B -m
.I mountpoint
]
[
.B -s
.I service
]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Aux/acpi
presents at
.I mountpoint
(default
.BR /dev )
an interface to the ACPI, and posts it at
.BI /srv/ service
(default
.BR acpi ).
The machine has one AML interpreter: if the service is posted
already (a GPU driver may have started it,
.IR gpu (4)),
.I aux/acpi
mounts it at
.I mountpoint
instead and exits.
.PP
With the
.B -H
option,
.I aux/acpi
will turn off the power immediately.
.PP
The directory contains the following files.
.TP
.B battery
Contains one line for each battery in the system.  Each line lists 14
fields: the percent charge remaining, power unit used (mW or mA),
remaining capacity, last full charge capacity, design capacity,
warning and low capacity values,
.BR "mV"
separator, present voltage, design voltage, approximate time of charge
left as
.BR hh:mm:ss ,
the status (a string, one of
.BR unknown ,
.BR critical ,
.BR discharging
or
.BR charging ) 
and the charge start and stop limits in percent.
.TP
.B cputemp
Each line provides a current temperature reading of a specific CPU.
.TP
.B pmctl
Writing
.I power off
to
.B pmctl
will turn off the power.
Writing 
.I charge bat min max
to
.B pmctl
will set the upper and lower limit for charging a battery. bat is either
.B "all"
for all batteries or starts with 0.
.TP
.B aml
The interpreter for other programs (the GPU drivers'
ACPI methods, see
.IR gpu (4));
only the host owner opens it.
A write is a request, a read on the same file descriptor its answer:
.RS
.TP
.BI eval " path nargs value" ...
the value of the object at
.I path
(of a method: its result, called with the arguments)
.TP
.BI walk " path name"
the path of
.I name
right below
.I path
.RB ( -
for the root; not found by the search rules higher up),
or of an absolute
.I name
.TP
.BI parent " path"
the scope above
.TP
.BI pci " bus dev fn"
the device of that PCI address, by
.B _ADR
.TP
.BI hid " path"
a device's
.B _HID
as text
.TP
.B devices
.RI ` path " " hid '
for every device with a
.B _HID
.RE
.IP
Paths are as
.IR aml (2)'s
.B %N
prints them
.RB ( \\_SB.PCI0.GFX0 ).
A value is
.B -
(none),
.BI i hex ;
(integer),
.BI s n : bytes
(string),
.BI b n : hex
(buffer of
.I n
bytes),
.BI p n :
followed by
.I n
values (package) or
.BI r n : path
(reference).
Operation regions in a PCI device's configuration space reach the
device through
.BR #$/pci .
.SH SOURCE
.B /sys/src/cmd/aux/acpi.c
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR reform (1)
.SH BUGS
ACPI itself.
.PP
There are too many ways for controlling battery charging. For now it only works on Thinkpads.
.SH HISTORY
.I Acpi
first appeared in 9front (October, 2016).
